Stage 1 provides no qualifying derived-lemma ordering: `prove.sh` compiles `verification.k` with all nine rules already present, then proves only the reachability claims. The two mutation specs are expected failures, not proofs of reusable rule statements. Therefore no inventory rule can be labeled `PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA`; all nine are definitional equations/recurrences, and the domain-lemma set is empty.
